# 2. PROJECT OVERVIEW

### Project name
AI-Powered Accessibility Assistant

### Problem statement

Visually impaired individuals frequently face difficulties reading printed information, understanding their surroundings, identifying Indian currency and independently interacting with everyday objects.

Existing accessibility solutions may require expensive devices, continuous internet connectivity or complicated interfaces.

The proposed application aims to provide an affordable, accessible and lightweight solution using artificial intelligence, computer vision and voice interaction.

### Main objective

Develop a mobile-friendly accessibility assistant that enables visually impaired users to interact with their surroundings through voice commands and audio feedback.

### Core features

**Feature 1: Multilingual Text Reading (OCR)**
- Capture printed text using the smartphone camera.
- Extract text using OCR.
- Support English, Hindi and Kannada.
- Read extracted text aloud.
- Detect the language automatically.
- Handle unclear or low-quality images.

**Feature 2: AI Scene Description**
- Capture an image of the surroundings.
- Generate a meaningful description of the scene.
- Describe visible objects and their arrangement when supported.
- Support English, Hindi and Kannada output.
- Provide audio descriptions.
- Warn users that descriptions may be inaccurate.

**Feature 3: Voice-Controlled Assistant**
- Operate the application without touching the screen whenever possible.
- Recognize English, Hindi and Kannada voice commands.
- Support hands-free interaction where browser capabilities permit.
- Provide push-to-talk as a fallback.
- Confirm every successfully recognized command through audio.

**Feature 4: Indian Currency Recognition**
- Recognize Indian rupee denominations:
  - ₹10
  - ₹20
  - ₹50
  - ₹100
  - ₹200
  - ₹500
  - ₹2000
- Use a lightweight image classification model.
- Perform inference offline on the device.
- Announce the predicted denomination through speech.
- Include an uncertain/unknown classification when confidence is insufficient.

Note: ₹2000 notes are included for recognition of existing notes, not because they remain in circulation as a regularly issued denomination.

