# 6. IMPORTANT DESIGN AND ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES

The final application must follow these principles:

### Accessibility first
The application must be usable by someone who cannot see the screen.

Never make colour, icons, images or visual indicators the only way to understand an action or status.

### Low-end device optimization
Prioritize:
- Small model sizes.
- Efficient image preprocessing.
- Lazy loading.
- Reduced memory usage.
- Minimal background processing.
- Battery-efficient operation.

### Offline-first design
Keep essential features available without internet connectivity wherever technically possible.

### Privacy by design
Do not retain user photographs unless the user explicitly chooses otherwise.

### Honest AI
Clearly communicate uncertainty and limitations.

### Maintainable architecture
Keep frontend, backend, AI models and evaluation scripts modular.

### Real-world usability
Optimize for actual accessibility requirements rather than merely making the application look attractive.

### Testing before claims
Do not claim accuracy, speed, reliability or device compatibility without testing.

